
Vital Event Registration and Management System (VERMS) for South Gondar Zone

VERMS is a web-based civil statistics platform designed to modernize and automate the manual, paper-based registration of critical vital events (birth, death, marriage, and divorce) across the hierarchical administrative layers of the South Gondar Zone in Amhara, Ethiopia.
This project was developed by Group 1 as partial fulfillment of the requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree in Information Technology at Debre Tabor University, Gafat Institute of Technology.

🚀 Key Features

• Tiered Architecture Access: Specialized web interfaces map to the real-world administrative hierarchy of Ethiopia (Kebele, Woreda, and Zone levels).
• Tamper-Evident Certification: Instantaneous production of secure PDF digital certificates complete with unique QR codes, digital officer signatures, and official administrative seals.
• Business Rule Automation (BR1 - BR11): Legal parameters are hardcoded directly into front/back-end verification filters, eliminating entry errors, handling dual-language documentation (Amharic & English), checking physical attendance states, and preventing duplicate registrations.
• Real-time Data Syncing: Distributed data capture allowing offline logging capabilities for remote Kebeles via field tablets, syncing automatically when wide-area networks or LAN links establish connectivity.
• On-Demand Demographics Reporting: Automated analytical engines empowering administrators and statisticians to compile localized mortality, fertility, and marital stability metrics in a single click.

🛠️ System Tech Stack

• Frontend UI/UX: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (Single-Page Application desktop-like experience optimization).
• Backend Architecture: PHP (structured server-side processing following the MVC pattern).
• Database Management: MySQL Relational Database Structure.
• Security Layer: Password hashing protocols, Input validation, Session lifecycle parameters, Multi-Factor Authentication frameworks, and TLS 1.2+ encrypted communication streams.

📂 Codebase Repository Tree

text
├── .github/workflows/      # CI/CD deployment logic & automations
├── admin/                  # Account configurations, permissions, and location tools
├── citizen/                # Front-facing request intakes and digital certificate tracking
├── kebele_officer/         # Primary frontline field data registries 
├── woreda_officer/         # District validation buffers, audit verification panels, and feedback loops
├── zone/                   # Central administration interface for regional coordination
├── Statistician/           # Central Statistics Agency analytic portals and metric counts
├── includes/               # Shared backend dependencies (`db_connection.php`, global fragments)
├── css/                    # Custom styling layouts (`style.css`)
├── js/                     # Component scripts (`script.js`)
├── index.php               # System runtime gateway (Role-aware entry point redirection)
├── login.php               # Secure role-based user authentication engine
└── logout.php              # Full session termination handlers
Use code with caution.

